{"kind":"article","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/SplittingAGameAcrossFiles","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"text":"Keep a large game readable by composing its map and rules from per-region helpers.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Gnusto"}],"title":"Splitting a Game Across Files","roleHeading":"Article"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/gnusto\/splittingagameacrossfiles"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Composing-Large-Games","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContentBundles","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Plugins","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameContent","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameContents","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GamePlugin"],"generated":true,"title":"Composing Large Games"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A Gnusto game is one type conforming to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Game","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". That does ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}]},{"text":" mean it must live in one file. A large game splits cleanly along two of its three parts today; the third has a known boundary worth understanding.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"The-one-rule-declarations-stay-in-the-struct-body","text":"The one rule: declarations stay in the struct body","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Locations, items, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Global"},{"type":"text","text":" state are "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"stored properties","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", and Swift requires stored properties to be declared in a type’s main body — not in an extension. The bootstrap also discovers every entity by reflecting over the single "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Game","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" type and naming each entity after its property ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"let foyer = Location { … }"},{"type":"text","text":" becomes "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/EntityID","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"foyer\""},{"type":"text","text":"). So all entity declarations live together, in the file that declares the struct:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct OperaHouse: Game {","    let foyer = Location { name(\"Foyer of the Opera House\"); … }","    let bar   = Location { name(\"Foyer Bar\"); dark }","    let cloak = Item { name(\"velvet cloak\"); wearable }","    @Global var disturbances = 0","    \/\/ …","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"(If you reach the point where even the ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"declarations","type":"text"}]},{"text":" need to span files or ship in a separate package, reach for ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"content bundles"}]},{"text":" — a region declared as its own ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameContent","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" type. See "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContentBundles","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":".)"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"`map` and `rules` compose across files","level":2,"anchor":"map-and-rules-compose-across-files","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Both ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rules"},{"type":"text","text":" are result-builder properties, and the builder accepts whole "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WorldMap","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Rules","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" values as well as individual entries. That means you can break each one into per-region helper properties and splice them together:"}]},{"code":["extension OperaHouse {","    var map: WorldMap {","        foyerMap        \/\/ a WorldMap, defined elsewhere","        cloakroomMap","        barMap","        player.starts(in: foyer)","    }","","    var rules: Rules {","        foyerRules      \/\/ a Rules value, defined elsewhere","        cloakroomRules","        barRules","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each helper is itself a builder property, annotated so its body can use the block syntax. Put each region in its own file:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ OperaHouse+Bar.swift","extension OperaHouse {","    @MapBuilder var barMap: WorldMap {","        bar.north(foyer)","        message.starts(in: bar)","    }","","    @RuleBuilder var barRules: Rules {","        bar.beforeEachTurn { … }","        bar.afterEachTurn  { … }","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Inside an extension, the bare identifiers ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bar"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"message","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"player","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"command"},{"text":", your ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Global"},{"text":"s) resolve to the same declarations and engine globals they would inside the struct — nothing needs to be passed around.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"A-recommended-layout-for-a-large-game","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"A recommended layout for a large game"},{"code":["MyGame\/","  MyGame.swift            \/\/ struct: all Location\/Item\/@Global declarations,","                          \/\/   plus map { … } and rules { … } that compose the regions","  MyGame+Foyer.swift      \/\/ foyerMap  + foyerRules","  MyGame+Cloakroom.swift  \/\/ cloakroomMap + cloakroomRules","  MyGame+Bar.swift        \/\/ barMap    + barRules"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":null},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The struct file stays a readable table of contents — what exists and how the regions connect — while each region’s geography and logic lives next to itself."}]},{"anchor":"Split-for-reading-not-for-the-stack","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Split for reading, not for the stack"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Split a ","type":"text"},{"code":"map","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or a ","type":"text"},{"code":"rules","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" body when it has stopped reading as one thing, and for no other reason. There is no size limit to keep under: ","type":"text"},{"code":"Bootstrap.build","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" runs on a thread the engine sizes at 16 MB, not on whatever stack it happened to be called from, so a game boots the same under ","type":"text"},{"code":"swift run","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as it does inside a test — where a Swift Testing body has only 512 KB of its own.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"That symmetry is the point of the fixed budget. Without it, a game grows until the "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"tests","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" die and the shipped binary does not, and the failure arrives as an unattributed signal that names no game, no bundle and no declaration. Gnusto’s own Dungeon spent four milestones paying for that: bodies split, then content deleted, against a cliff nobody could measure."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If you ever want the measurement rather than the assurance, set ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GNUSTO_STACK_REPORT"},{"text":" and the boot prints what it used:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["$ GNUSTO_STACK_REPORT=1 swift run Dungeon","Gnusto: Dungeon bootstrapped using 340 KB of the 16384 KB bootstrap stack."],"type":"codeListing","syntax":null},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Dungeon is 23 content bundles and some 800 declarations, so 340 KB is a useful sense of scale: a game would have to be an order of magnitude larger before the figure was worth looking at. (The same game reports about 355 KB from inside ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swift test"},{"text":", because a test bundle is built with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-enable-testing"},{"text":" and its frames are a little wider. Both are the same bootstrap on the same 16 MB worker.)","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Worked example","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Worked-example"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tests\/GnustoTests\/Support\/SplitGame\/"},{"text":" is a minimal game authored exactly this way: declarations in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SplitGame.swift"},{"text":", with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"gardenMap"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"gardenRules"},{"text":" in ","type":"text"},{"code":"SplitGame+Garden.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"houseMap"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"houseRules"},{"type":"text","text":" in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SplitGame+House.swift"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MultiFileCompositionTests"},{"type":"text","text":" boots it and confirms that the map entries and rules from every file take effect at runtime."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"What-splits-and-how","level":2,"text":"What splits, and how"},{"header":"row","type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Part"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Splits across files?"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rules"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Yes — compose from per-region ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Rules","type":"reference"},{"text":" helpers.","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes — compose from per-region "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WorldMap","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" helpers."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Custom verbs","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes — a game’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"verbs"},{"type":"text","text":" block, and any bundle’s."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Entity declarations"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In the struct body by default; across types\/packages via "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContentBundles","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]]]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The table above is the extension-based split: one "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Game","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" struct, declarations in its body, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"rules","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"verbs","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" composed from per-region helpers. When a region needs to own its "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"declarations"}]},{"type":"text","text":" too — or ship as a package — promote it to a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContentBundles"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"references":{"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Game":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Game"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Game"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Game","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A complete game: declarations, geography, and rules.","type":"text"}],"title":"Game","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/game","type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto","title":"Gnusto","abstract":[{"text":"A Swift engine for writing parser-driven interactive fiction — text adventures in the tradition of Zork and Infocom’s ZIL.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/WorldMap":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"WorldMap","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WorldMap","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WorldMap","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The geography and initial placements of a game, declared in one block:"}],"title":"WorldMap","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/worldmap","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/GamePlugin":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/gameplugin","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GamePlugin","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A reusable game system — commerce, combat, dialog, magic — packaged as an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"importable unit of "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"verbs","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"rules","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", that a host game opts into."}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"GamePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"GamePlugin","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"GamePlugin","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/GameContent":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"GameContent","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"GameContent","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameContent","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A self-contained slice of a game’s world: its own rooms, items, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Global"},{"type":"text","text":" state, plus the geography, rules, and verbs that go with them."}],"title":"GameContent","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/gamecontent","type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Plugins":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/plugins","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Plugins","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Package a reusable game system as an importable unit of verbs and rules."}],"title":"Plugins","role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/ContentBundles":{"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContentBundles","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Give a region its own declarations — its own type, and even its own package.","type":"text"}],"title":"Content Bundles","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/contentbundles"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/GameContents":{"title":"GameContents","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameContents","abstract":[{"text":"The collected content bundles a game declares, in declaration order.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/gamecontents","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"GameContents"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"GameContents"}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Rules":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/rules","type":"topic","title":"Rules","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Rules"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Rules"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Rules","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The collected rules of a game, declared in one ","type":"text"},{"code":"rules","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" block. Large games","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"compose: "},{"code":"var rules: Rules { cloakRules; barRules }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/EntityID":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/EntityID","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A stable, human-readable entity name derived from the Swift property label","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"at registration time (","type":"text"},{"code":"let bar = Location { … }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" → ","type":"text"},{"code":"EntityID(\"bar\")","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityID","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityID","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"EntityID","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/entityid"}}}